  "theorems": [
    "The exact t-away singleton complement has unique reduced degree (N+1)(p-1) if p does not divide N and N(p-1) otherwise, with individual degree p-1 in every coordinate.",
    "The t-away incidence-<L complement has reduced degree at least (N-L+2)(p-1), and the externally t-restricted row function has lower bound (N-L+1)(p-1).",
    "The integral triangular load recurrence preserves the row-only degree before endpoint and canonical-box specialization.",
    "The actual candidate loop product gcd(p,Phi_p(t,Z)) equals U_11 exactly, but each hit-specific canonical lift is at least p^(p-1), yielding aggregate height at least A log U_11.",
    "At a singleton Phi_p/p is minus the moving Fermat quotient modulo p; the family t=1, rows=(p,p-1) has valuation exactly one for every odd p."
